cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the associated article below.
title: >-
  Optimizing Heat Flux Density for Solar Tower Power Plants:
  A Novel HFLCAL Linearization Approach
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a convex aim-point correction method for solar
  tower power plants with cylindrical receivers. Linearizing the HFLCAL flux
  model about a structurally misaligned aim-point configuration turns flux
  shaping under a hard allowable-flux-density constraint into a quadratic
  program, solved to global optimality of the linearized problem over all
  5,300 correction variables at full Gemasolar scale.
